Subject: [PATCH] pgfuzz CI: a marker proving the patch pipeline ran

WHY THIS EXISTS.

A workspace can declare `patch=`, and until this repository's audit nothing
applied it -- the code was written, tested and called by nobody. It is wired
now, and the only thing standing between that and the next silent regression is
a test that a real patch reaches a real build.

Vendor patches cannot serve: they are not ours to ship, they target one minor
version, and they rewrite planner behaviour. This one adds a FILE THAT NOTHING
COMPILES, so it applies cleanly to every major from 16 to master and cannot
change what is built. What it proves is the pipeline: the series applied, no
.rej survived, the patch was hashed into the build record, and the inventory
can name it.

If this file is missing from a built tree, the patch step did not run.
---
 src/pgfuzz_ci_marker.txt | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 src/pgfuzz_ci_marker.txt

diff --git a/src/pgfuzz_ci_marker.txt b/src/pgfuzz_ci_marker.txt
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..1111111
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/pgfuzz_ci_marker.txt
@@ -0,0 +1,7 @@
+pgfuzz CI patch marker.
+
+This file is added by project/patches/0001-ci-marker.patch so that CI can
+prove a workspace patch series was applied to the tree that was built.
+
+Nothing compiles it. If it is absent from a build whose workspace declares
+patch=, the patch step did not run.
